  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">STRENGTHENING INDIGENOUS CONSERVATION CAPACITY TO PROTECT PERU S PUR S MANU LANDSCAPE</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">THE PURPOSE OF THIS PROJECT IS TO STRENGTHEN INDIGENOUS CONSERVATION CAPACITY IN PERUS YURA, INUYA, AND SEPAHUA WATERSHEDS IN ORDER TO PROTECT THREATENED ECOSYSTEMS, ENDANGERED SPECIES AND HABITATS, AND THE WAY OF LIFE OF THE SETTLED AND ISOLATED INDIGENOUS TRIBES WHO LIVE THERE. THESE RIVERS PROVIDE ACCESS TO THE 10-MILLION-HECTARE PURS MANU LANDSCAPE, WHICH CONTAINS SOME OF THE MOST REMOTE AND LEAST DISTURBED FORESTS IN THE ENTIRE AMAZON BASIN. HOWEVER, ALL THREE WATERSHEDS ARE CRITICALLY THREATENED BY ROAD CONSTRUCTION, ILLEGAL LOGGING, AND LAND TRAFFICKING FACILITATED BY THE LOGGER-NARCO MAFIA THAT HAS AGGRESSIVELY MOVED INTO THESE REMOTE LOWLAND FORESTS OVER THE PAST FEW YEARS.WE WILL WORK WITH PERUS PARKS SERVICE, SERNANP, INDIGENOUS FEDERATIONS AND ASSOCIATIONS, AND INDIVIDUAL COMMUNITIES ON MEASURES THAT WILL PROMOTE MORE EFFECTIVE COMMUNITY VIGILANCE, IMPROVED PROTECTED AREA MANAGEMENT, SPECIES CONSERVATION, SUSTAINABLE RESOURCE USE, AND ADAPTATION TO CLIMATE CHANGE. OBJECTIVES AND ACTIVITIES INCLUDE: (1) STRENGTHEN THE VIGILANCE CAPACITY OF EIGHT STRATEGICALLY-LOCATED COMMUNITIES BY PROVIDING EQUIPMENT, CONDUCTING REGULAR PATROLS, AND INTRODUCING THE SMART MONITORING TECHNOLOGY (2) IMPROVE THE MANAGEMENT EFFECTIVENESS OF THE YURA COMMUNAL CONSERVATION CONCESSION THROUGH VIGILANCE AND ADMINISTRATION T</narrative>
  </description>
